	"identifying_description": "Leaf of paper with watercolor, ink, and gold leaf with illustration of Hymen holding a blazing torch and leading a wedding procession at center .As couple approach the altar, the goddess Aphrodite hands down a floral crown. In the lateral extensions appear Abundance, at right, and Prudence, at left. Plain on reverse with garlands. Sticks and guards of carved mother-of-pearl and ivory with applied silver leaf. Glass jewel and copper alloy rivet.",
	"web_text": "Illustrations of Hymen, the god of marriage, kindling a marital fire before a bride and groom often appear on wedding fans made throughout the eighteenth century. The well-proportioned and symmetrical arrangement of this fan's design reveals the influence of classical art and antiquities on late eighteenth-century visual arts.",
	"didactic_label": "Illustrations of Hymen, the god of marriage, kindling a marital fire before a bride and groom often appear on wedding fans made throughout the eighteenth century. The well-proportioned and symmetrical arrangement of this fan's design reveals the influence of classical art and antiquities on late eighteenth-century visual arts.",
